{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1392923-other-worlds-and-aliens-in-scion","id":1392923,"title":"Other Worlds and aliens in Scion?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-05-30T15:37:03-07:00","id":1392923,"title":"Other Worlds and aliens in Scion?","content":"So the gods created this World that humans live in and created humanity. What I haven't seen though in the books is a discussion of what other worlds and intelligent creatures might have been created by the gods.<br /> <br /> Have any of you thought about the possibilities for this? What would aliens worship, for example? And are there other planets like earth that the gods have created?<br /> <br /> Sorry for spamming lots of questions in this forum, but the gameworld of Scion fascinates me too much.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9849-aristarkos","name":"Aristarkos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9849_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-30T16:29:50-07:00","id":1392931,"title":"","content":"When you look at the stories told about and attitudes taken toward aliens, they've clearly part of the spiritual ecosystem. &quot;Space Brothers&quot; are often interchangeable with angels. Many traits of the faeries are typical of the &quot;aliens.&quot; The &quot;Nordics&quot; equate to elves or sidhe. Greys equate with goblins and the Norse Dwarfs that were born from the magots that crawled on Ymir's corpse. The Reptilians equate to such beings as the Italian Orcos and Orchulis, and the Arabs Ghouls and Jinni. <br /> <br /> As what the 1st ed called &quot;Lesser Immortals&quot; and the present edition calls denizens, the Aliens probably worship distinctive aspects of the better known gods.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-30T16:42:56-07:00","id":1392935,"title":"","content":"Alternatively, with the new Companion coming out, you could give the Aliens a Pantheon (or more) of their own.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/665-shkspr1048","name":"shkspr1048","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"630"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-30T18:44:27-07:00","id":1392970,"title":"","content":"Given \u00c6on and its supplements also use the Storypath system, it shouldn't be too hard to convert 'em over to Scion rules if you were of a mind to do so.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-30T19:36:30-07:00","id":1392977,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1392923-other-worlds-and-aliens-in-scion?p=1392931#post1392931\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When you look at the stories told about and attitudes taken toward aliens, they've clearly part of the spiritual ecosystem. &quot;Space Brothers&quot; are often interchangeable with angels. Many traits of the faeries are typical of the &quot;aliens.&quot; The &quot;Nordics&quot; equate to elves or sidhe. Greys equate with goblins and the Norse Dwarfs that were born from the magots that crawled on Ymir's corpse. The Reptilians equate to such beings as the Italian Orcos and Orchulis, and the Arabs Ghouls and Jinni.<br /> <br /> As what the 1st ed called &quot;Lesser Immortals&quot; and the present edition calls denizens, the Aliens probably worship distinctive aspects of the better known gods.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd be very careful with these kinds of connections. Like, the whole Ancient Aliens thing is a theory that while superficially Neat is a little reductionist, rather imperialist, and a LOT racist. But that's a whole thing I won't dig too deep into, so instead I'll just say this:<br /> <br /> I'm all for aliens in Scion. But I wouldn't attribute any Gods or other legendary being to their presence. Unless like, aliens land and turns out they worship Durga too, that'd be pretty funny. But I wouldn't go around saying &quot;Oh yeah, these Gods, these Denizens, these animal folk? Aliens. Totally.&quot; I'd want the aliens to bring their on myth with them, maybe Gods we never imagined. Go really ALIEN with them, rather than going &quot;And the Fae are aliens&quot;.<br /> <br /> Also just as an FYI, the Reptilians conspiracy theory, AFAIK, has basically nothing to do with any previous gods and have everything to do with rampant anti-Semetism. So while lizardfolks are fine, making them a massive cabal of all-knowing inhuman monsters who secretly control the world governments as most people refer to 'Reptilians' isn't a take I like to get too close to.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-30T19:50:49-07:00","id":1392982,"title":"","content":"Well, technically, if the Aesir are from Asgard, they are aliens. So any being from another world (or nine) or another dimension (such as a Godrealm) would be an &quot;alien&quot; by definition. It really isn't disrespectful or far-fetched to use the term when referring to such beings ; I've always done it in my campaign. It doen't have to mean &quot;little grey humanoid in a flying saucer.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5627-purple-snit","name":"Purple Snit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5627_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"309"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-30T19:54:37-07:00","id":1392984,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1392923-other-worlds-and-aliens-in-scion?p=1392977#post1392977\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'd be very careful with these kinds of connections. Like, the whole Ancient Aliens thing is a theory that while superficially Neat is a little reductionist, rather imperialist, and a LOT racist. But that's a whole thing I won't dig too deep into, so instead I'll just say this:<br /> <br /> I'm all for aliens in Scion. But I wouldn't attribute any Gods or other legendary being to their presence. Unless like, aliens land and turns out they worship Durga too, that'd be pretty funny. But I wouldn't go around saying &amp;quot;Oh yeah, these Gods, these Denizens, these animal folk? Aliens. Totally.&amp;quot; I'd want the aliens to bring their on myth with them, maybe Gods we never imagined. Go really ALIEN with them, rather than going &amp;quot;And the Fae are aliens&amp;quot;.<br /> <br /> Also just as an FYI, the Reptilians conspiracy theory, AFAIK, has basically nothing to do with any previous gods and have everything to do with rampant anti-Semetism. So while lizardfolks are fine, making them a massive cabal of all-knowing inhuman monsters who secretly control the world governments as most people refer to 'Reptilians' isn't a take I like to get too close to.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was describing the creatures the &quot;space brothers&quot; get treated as in popular and folk culture. I've heard country western songs from as far back as the 1950s that treat UFOs as signs of the apocalypse and/or angels.<br /> <br /> Folklorists have been comparing &quot;aliens&quot; and cryptids to the fairies for decades. It's nearly a commonplace.<br /> <br /> The powers, attitudes, and other motifs of the reptilians are very much like the Italian and Arab fay I mentioned. It's an unconscious recycling of older tropes.<br /> <br /> I'm not saying that these are the old tales reworked, although I often think that, but the &quot;aliens&quot; of fiction, folk belief, etc. recycle old tropes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-30T19:55:13-07:00","id":1392985,"title":"","content":"I would be very careful on Alien worshipping the same gods, unless you use a Iron/Heroic Theocentric focused on a single pantheon that have mantles in other cultures (including aliens).<br /> <br /> Lets day you have people in alpha Centauri worshiping the Kami, how would they know the Kami if not even the European continent (a few hundred thousand kilometer away) knew them a century or so ago.<br /> <br /> I don\u2019t mean it\u2019s impossible, but... would be weird.<br /> <br /> Anyway, If I were going to run a Scion campaign on space, I would go on a Star Gate approach, but the gods being real (not technology users, but really divine). I would use the pantheons as factions (some closer, some more distant) conquering worlds for worshipers and Legend, and Earth would be one world that were occupied by several pantheons during the history.<br /> <br /> I didn\u2019t think a lot about it, but that would be my general approach of the subject.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-30T20:15:08-07:00","id":1392989,"title":"","content":"I think it would be easy enough to borrow the Atlantean PSP and Motif to lean into New Gods sufficiently advanced alien options.<br /> <br /> The Masks is the Mythos book should be hackable to do a much more... alien... alien pantheon.<br /> <br /> I\u2019ve considered trying my hand at a Planetary Romance \u201cMartian\u201d Pantheon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-30T20:32:51-07:00","id":1392993,"title":"","content":"I'd follow a harder line; if aliens worship gods, then those gods are alien.<br /> Of course this thread now has me imagining a Scion game where first contact happens and the major players on both sides consider the other to be abombinations on par with the Titanmachy.<br /> Interstellar holy war on par with the Covenant from Halo on the mundane side, literal alien demigods trying to destroy the Earth pantheons, just as Julius did to the Nementondevos.<br /> <br /> Though I do agree with Ian Watson; Trinity is right there. Take their alien building rules, create aliens. Then add Scion template <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-30T22:22:38-07:00","id":1393006,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1392923-other-worlds-and-aliens-in-scion?p=1392984#post1392984\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I was describing the creatures the &quot;space brothers&quot; get treated as in popular and folk culture. I've heard country western songs from as far back as the 1950s that treat UFOs as signs of the apocalypse and/or angels.<br /> <br /> Folklorists have been comparing &quot;aliens&quot; and cryptids to the fairies for decades. It's nearly a commonplace.</div> </div> </div> </div>Shockingly, going &quot;But they've been doing this for decades&quot; in no way sidesteps, erases, or denies the things I noted. That just means that some people have been doing it for like, less than a century?<br /> <br /> And I'm not saying don't do it, I'm just saying that you gotta be really effing careful or else you may fall face-first into &quot;Obviously the Pyramids were built by aliens because those primitive brown people could never figure out MATH&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The powers, attitudes, and other motifs of the reptilians are very much like the Italian and Arab fay I mentioned. It's an unconscious recycling of older tropes.<br /> <br /> I'm not saying that these are the old tales reworked, although I often think that, but the &quot;aliens&quot; of fiction, folk belief, etc. recycle old tropes. </div> </div> </div>Okay we may be thinking of different Reptilians in pop culture, let me just list the trappings I'm familiar with. Are you talking about lizard hybrids that:<ul><li>Have infiltrated/interbred with human bloodlines?</li> <li>The same bloodlines that coincidentally show up in royal families and influential American lines or as popular figures?</li> <li>Hide their reptilian features either through skin suits or through a kind of hypnotic psionic hypnosis signal</li> <li>Through their infiltration work in a secret cabal organizing every aspect of the world governments to usher in a New World Order?</li> </ul>Because those may be kind of sort of like these beings that you mentioned by coincidence, but they were mostly very deliberately drawing on VERY anti-Semetic conspiracy theories, dehumanizing Jewish people by making them out to be alien beings (lizardlike monsters that pretend to be human) that control the world governments (harkening to the Zionist Conspiracies). So, no, the modern pop culture Reptilian conspiracies in no way call back to any lizard creatures that may or may not have existed in Italian folklore, but they do VERY DELIBERATELY parrot talking points of anti-Semetic white nationalist dog whistles.<br /> <br /> Now to make it very explicit: I'm not saying that you're deliberately perpetuating these. These get cloaked just enough so that those on the outside don't recognize them and get perpetuated that way. That's how they sneak this shit into popular consumption without people realizing. That's why it's important to recognize these smokescreens and dogwhistles so that you go &quot;Hey wait a minute-&quot; if someone tries to push them too hard.<br /> <br /> Also, on the 'They recycle old tropes'... Scion 2e is not a game that's well served by going Campbellian Monomyth. Never was. Never should be. It only gets better when you're NOT going &quot;Yeah y'know what A is B is C&quot; and I think it's massively reductionist and just flat-out wrong to go &quot;Well if you look at the broadest of terms the Greys are Goblins are Nordic Dwarves&quot;. They're really not. Like, at all. Unless your definition of all they have in common is &quot;Short&quot;.<br /> <br /> Edit: That got a bit intense. So yes: Aliens. Very much approve. Building them can come from say, persistent Conditions and maybe some situational Enhancement, mixed with custom Paths.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":2142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","user":"Kyman201","date":". 05-31-2020, 02:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-30T22:36:55-07:00","id":1393008,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FallenEco</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1392923-other-worlds-and-aliens-in-scion?p=1392993#post1392993\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Though I do agree with Ian Watson; Trinity is right there. Take their alien building rules, create aliens. Then add Scion template <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I'm looking through the book for rules on building aliens but find none. On what page are they?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9849-aristarkos","name":"Aristarkos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9849_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-30T22:52:05-07:00","id":1393010,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aristarkos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1392923-other-worlds-and-aliens-in-scion?p=1393008#post1393008\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm looking through the book for rules on building aliens but find none. On what page are they?</div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair; the rules for <i>playable aliens</i> are supposed to be in an upcoming book (Under Alien Suns). Non-Player aliens follow npc rules in the antagonist section...so it isn't much help right now. That said, I expect to get UAS before Demigod gets kickstarted anyway, so I wasn't exactly expecting to rush anyway.<br /> Sorry <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9849-aristarkos\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar9849_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"9849\" data-vbnamecard=\"9849\">Aristarkos</a>, I didn't mean to mislead you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-31T00:02:23-07:00","id":1393021,"title":"","content":"Some playable aliens are in Distant Worlds, but yes, more robust alien-creation rules are in Under Alien Suns.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-31T06:03:51-07:00","id":1393068,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1392923-other-worlds-and-aliens-in-scion?p=1393006#post1393006\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Shockingly, going &quot;But they've been doing this for decades&quot; in no way sidesteps, erases, or denies the things I noted. That just means that some people have been doing it for like, less than a century?</div> </div> </div> </div>Read the book &quot;Passport to Magonia.&quot; From the 1960s, the UFO believers had it as a commonplace then. I've read, but no longer remember the authors, articles from the late 1950s claiming to show that the &quot;Space Brothers&quot; were simply a reworking of the faeries. I read these in the 1980s in an even then defunct journal of folklore studies. So, I apologize if I was too brusque, but folklore dealing with spirits, fay, ghosts, etc. is one of my things.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And I'm not saying don't do it, I'm just saying that you gotta be really effing careful or else you may fall face-first into &quot;Obviously the Pyramids were built by aliens because those primitive brown people could never figure out MATH&quot; </div> </div> </div>Like Carl Sagan, who championed the theories of <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Iosif_Shklovsky\" target=\"_blank\">Shlovsky</a>, I loathe that racist hack <b>von D\u00e4niken. </b>But saying that the &quot;aliens&quot; are the fay doesn't require any of that. From a strictly folkloric point of view, it's simply a new term hooked up with old tropes/stories.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Okay we may be thinking of different Reptilians in pop culture, let me just list the trappings I'm familiar with. Are you talking about lizard hybrids that:<ul><li>Have infiltrated/interbred with human bloodlines?</li> <li>The same bloodlines that coincidentally show up in royal families and influential American lines or as popular figures?</li> <li>Hide their reptilian features either through skin suits or through a kind of hypnotic psionic hypnosis signal</li> <li>Through their infiltration work in a secret cabal organizing every aspect of the world governments to usher in a New World Order?</li> </ul> </div> </div> </div>Number three fits well with Orcos, Orchi, Ghuls, and Jinni, all being masters of disguise. Certainly, all of these creatures are malignant tricksters. Kidnapping human women to breed with is also a trope. It's the same old story reworked with conspiracy theories and sci-fi touches.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Because those may be kind of sort of like these beings that you mentioned by coincidence, but they were mostly very deliberately drawing on VERY anti-Semetic conspiracy theories, dehumanizing Jewish people by making them out to be alien beings (lizardlike monsters that pretend to be human) that control the world governments (harkening to the Zionist Conspiracies). So, no, the modern pop culture Reptilian conspiracies in no way call back to any lizard creatures that may or may not have existed in Italian folklore, but they do VERY DELIBERATELY parrot talking points of anti-Semetic white nationalist dog whistles. </div> </div> </div>As racism is a pseudoscientific idea it isn't odd that it would get blended in with superstition and malevolent nonsense. When <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Carl_Linnaeus\" target=\"_blank\">Carl Linnaeus</a>, a deeply racist man, created a human racial classification system, no bigots cared. It was flawed science, but it was science, so they couldn't use it. When the passionately anti-racist <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Johann_Friedrich_Blumenbach\" target=\"_blank\">Johann Friedrich Blumenbach</a> created a racial classification system to show we all descended from Adam and Eve, therefore, both racism and social class hierarchies were evil, racists jumped on his pseudoscience and ran with it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Now to make it very explicit: I'm not saying that you're deliberately perpetuating these. These get cloaked just enough so that those on the outside don't recognize them and get perpetuated that way. That's how they sneak this shit into popular consumption without people realizing. That's why it's important to recognize these smokescreens and dogwhistles so that you go &quot;Hey wait a minute-&quot; if someone tries to push them too hard. </div> </div> </div>Point taken with respect. Might I suggest you read <a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Strange-Secret-Peoples-Victorian-Consciousness/dp/0195144112\" target=\"_blank\">Strange and Secret Peoples</a>. There is an example of how brutal racism and faerie lore blend in a toxic confection. Nancy Silver, the author, shows how the description of a <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Baka_people_(Cameroon_and_Gabon)\" target=\"_blank\">Baka Chief</a> didn't match the photograph. The Baka are fairly attractive on the whole, and the photograph was of a pleasant looking young man. The description of the photo by the editor of the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Times\" target=\"_blank\">Times</a> was of a grotesque goblin and in no way matched the photograph. Ms. Silver scoured the Times letter columns for weeks afterward, no one seemed to notice the difference.<br /> <br /> Much of later 19th early 20th-century antisemitic literature draws on the tropes of goblins and witches to describe and define the Jewish peoples. Any cross-comparison of images of goblins with period images of the Jewish people and you find that as the decades rolled by toward the Holocaust you'll see the two sets of images becoming more alike. Faeries are an &quot;Other&quot; and one group of the &quot;not we&quot; easily gets blended into another. The very dehumanization I hear you objecting to.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, on the 'They recycle old tropes'... Scion 2e is not a game that's well served by going Campbellian Monomyth. Never was. Never should be. It only gets better when you're NOT going &quot;Yeah y'know what A is B is C&quot; and I think it's massively reductionist and just flat-out wrong to go &quot;Well if you look at the broadest of terms the Greys are Goblins are Nordic Dwarves&quot;. They're really not. Like, at all. Unless your definition of all they have in common is &quot;Short&quot;.<br /> <br /> Edit: That got a bit intense. So yes: Aliens. Very much approve. Building them can come from say, persistent Conditions and maybe some situational Enhancement, mixed with custom Paths. </div> </div> </div>Campbell's reputation got trashed because he called out <a href=\"https://artsfuse.org/102739/fuse-book-review-little-lamb-who-tried-to-kill-thee-exploring-the-story-of-abraham-and-isaac\" target=\"_blank\"> Martin Buber</a> for racism. Frankly, Buber denied that either the Native Americans or the Hindus were capable of real religious feelings. He also sneeringly denied the human equality of the Palestinians. Campbell was right to call him on these things. And were Buber was public and proud in his bigotries, the most they can accuse Campbell of is secret bigotries and reading suspect authors like Nietzsche or Ezra Pound.<br /> <br /> Moreover I equated the Greys to Norse Dwarves, I didn't claim identity. Vampires and the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gancanagh\" target=\"_blank\"> Gancanagh</a> and the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Leanan_s%C3%ADdhe\" target=\"_blank\">Leanan Sidhe</a> all get lumped together as supernatural beings that drain the life from others, which is a valid comparison. But such a comparison doesn't erase or deny the differences.<br /> <br /> We clearly have different intellectual backgrounds and experiences. We should share insights and information, not accuse each other of heresy and bigotry.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":857,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","user":"Astromancer","date":". 05-31-2020, 02:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-31T10:06:31-07:00","id":1393129,"title":"","content":"This notion that Astromancer is describing strikes me as being more appropriate for the likes of TC:\u00c6gis (where seemingly supernatural ideas are recast as sci-fi elements) than for Scion. <br /> <br /> For Scion, a Pantheon reflects (or is reflected by) a particular culture; and while the stereotypical approach with aliens is for each alien race to have a single culture, I would much prefer any aliens in Scion to have a lot more cultural diversity than that: multiple cultures per alien species. I also wouldn't expect any of those alien cultures to be similar enough to human cultures to share our Pantheons, at least not at first: the alien cultures should have their own alien Pantheons. <br /> <br /> That said, not every worshipper of the Aesir is Norse, not is every follower of the Theoi Greek. I expect that after First Contact, you'll start to get aliens who join human religions and vice versa; and once that happens, you'll start getting alien Scions of humanity's Pantheons and human Scions of the aliens' Pantheons \u2014 and eventually, all the other overlapping that exists between different Pantheons.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-31T10:56:14-07:00","id":1393141,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1392923-other-worlds-and-aliens-in-scion?p=1393129#post1393129\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This notion that Astromancer is describing strikes me as being more appropriate for the likes of TC:\u00c6gis (where seemingly supernatural ideas are recast as sci-fi elements) than for Scion.<br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>If you mean, by the &quot;Idea Astromancer is describing.&quot; that I'm suggesting a strict use of real-world historical president to define Scion, that's not what I propose. I offered the possibility of modeling some aspects of Aliens in the Scion setting on playing around with some real world presidents as long as they're fun. The one is an order the other is an invitation to self-aware play.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-31T11:10:01-07:00","id":1393146,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1392923-other-worlds-and-aliens-in-scion?p=1393141#post1393141\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you mean, by the &quot;Idea Astromancer is describing.&quot; that I'm suggesting a strict use of real-world historical precedent to define Scion, that's not what I propose.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not what I mean. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1392923-other-worlds-and-aliens-in-scion?p=1393141#post1393141\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I offered the possibility of modeling some aspects of Aliens in the Scion setting on playing around with some real world precedents as long as they're fun. The one is an order the other is an invitation to self-aware play.</div> </div> </div> </div>True, but not related to what I was saying.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-31T13:13:30-07:00","id":1393177,"title":"","content":"I do see some interesting potential in exploring the connection between mythic and extraterrestrial figures, but like people have pointed out, it's tricky to do that without falling into the trap of invalidating whatever mythologies you are using. Personally, I would turn the whole thing on its head. I'd like to think that in the World there are just as many UFO conspiracists as in our's and people quite reasonably dismiss their theories about crop circles and lights in the sky, because: &quot;Those are just fairies, you dummy! Just offer them some milk, don't make any promises to them, and they'll leave you alone.&quot;<br /> <br /> Jokes aside, though, I'm curious: Why are people thinking about adding aliens to a game about mythology? I'm not asking to be dismissive, I'm genuinely curious. Personally, what interests me about aliens in science fiction stories is seeing humanity confronted with something radically other than itself and how that challenges our perspective of ourselves. The more alien the aliens are, the better. I don't think that theme would translate to the setting of Scion in particular. Every single person in the World is already confronted with the fact that their whole existence is predicated on hundreds of mutually contradictory mythic realities overlapping with one another in a way that doesn't always make sense, but hey, it seems to work out fine. With everything going on in all those cosmologies, gray men from the sky seem rather underwhelming.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Pantheon:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1d6MGe0uK0nLsOABBu3YymfU-7gS7Nwur/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Th\u1ea7n of Vietnam</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25842-mr-wopsle","name":"Mr Wopsle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25842_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-31T18:06:54-07:00","id":1393277,"title":"","content":"I admit that if I were to go Full Space Opera with Scion, I'd be focusing less on aliens (though if I did I'd be making them mostly separate and maybe make some Gods for them) and more on what happens when a Hero goes Cosmic.<br /> <br /> Like, I'd want to run adventures about Tuatha longboats sailing among the stars, or intrepid Heroes dipping into the Otherworld and finding out that if you go into THIS forest in Ireland and follow this path through the Otherworld, you come out on a forest on another human colony. Yeah it takes a week for you to make the trip, and you're gone from the mortal World for like three months in Earth Time, but given that the colony is like over 20 lightyears away <i>that's one heck of a shortcut</i>.<br /> <br /> I'd want to run adventures of a group of Heroes who are using a variety of Marvels and spells to slowly terraform a new colony.<br /> <br /> <i>I want to run a story about the massive Teotl temple-ships that can use the offering of a heart in the main focus chamber to re-ignite a dying star</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-31T19:24:27-07:00","id":1393297,"title":"","content":"Hm, if i had to do a space themed story in scion i would have a god tier campaign where the earth got blown up and the scions, now gods, have to find the earth fragment and put the earth back together.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Completed campaign: Scion 2nd Edition. Les L\u00e9gendes Currently playing: Being a dad for a 3 year old daughter and a 2 years old son and now a beautiful new baby.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11312-maitrecorbo","name":"Maitrecorbo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11312_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"719"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-31T19:49:37-07:00","id":1393306,"title":"","content":"Kinda puts the Atlanteans' doom in a different light\u2026","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-03T13:12:20-07:00","id":1393835,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1392923-other-worlds-and-aliens-in-scion?p=1393068#post1393068\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Campbell's reputation got trashed because he called out <a href=\"https://artsfuse.org/102739/fuse-book-review-little-lamb-who-tried-to-kill-thee-exploring-the-story-of-abraham-and-isaac\" target=\"_blank\"> Martin Buber</a> for racism. Frankly, Buber denied that either the Native Americans or the Hindus were capable of real religious feelings. He also sneeringly denied the human equality of the Palestinians. Campbell was right to call him on these things. And were Buber was public and proud in his bigotries, the most they can accuse Campbell of is secret bigotries and reading suspect authors like Nietzsche or Ezra Pound.</div> </div> </div> </div>Regardless of anyone\u2019s relative character as a person, the Monomyth hypothesis has been thoroughly shredded by field anthropological work and archeological research for decades now. Campbell\u2019s work\u2019s lasting power is in media due to the usefulness of the Hero\u2019s Journey structure, and has influenced great works of fiction and media/lit study. I\u2019ve got Murdock\u2019s \u201cHeroine\u2019s Journey\u201d at my bedside currently (the Jungian psychological statements about human nature are unsurprisingly nonsense, but from the perspective of \u201chow cultural views on womanhood and the shared experience of women in western society shapes their narratives\u201d it\u2019s great!). From an anthropology/archeology/history standpoint though, his theories are swiftly approaching Golden Bough level out of date.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-03T13:56:19-07:00","id":1393851,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1392923-other-worlds-and-aliens-in-scion?p=1393068#post1393068\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">the most they can accuse Campbell of is secret bigotries and reading suspect authors like Nietzsche or Ezra Pound.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just to lean in, have you ever read Campbell's work Astromancer? Because quite literally the first clause of the first sentence of <i>The Hero With A Thousand Faces </i>is just flatly racist, and other issues show up through the entire book. As someone who studies heroes for a living, Campbell's work hasn't been seriously used in nearly half a century in actual academic works on the topic. Even for people wanting to use Heroic Biography models, they use Jan de Vries and he was an actual fucking Nazi. Like, self acclaimed and published under a pen name and all that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Campbell</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Whether we listen with aloof amusement to the dreamlike mumbo jumbo of some red-eyed witch doctor of the Congo</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","user":"Watcher","date":". 06-03-2020, 05:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-03T15:22:26-07:00","id":1393862,"title":"","content":"I've read about two-thirds of his books. And as a history major (my Masters is in History, poverty and poor health stopped me from going further) I'm highly aware of how quickly views of race and gender have evolved in the USA. Campbell was loudly telling scholars that dismissed non-Western religious beliefs as primitive and rudimentary that many of these spiritual paths were at least as rich and profound as their own. <br /> <br /> Campbell came from a cultural background that was known for &quot;gentile bigotry&quot; (how do those words go together?) His life clearly shows a man moving away from such things all of his life. <br /> <br /> Also, anyone who looks at the history of what we now call things like &quot;culture studies&quot; or &quot;anthropology&quot; that there is always an swaying back and forth between human unity and separation. Generally you start with someone calling for people to see human unity and brotherhood (and their theories get hijacked by racists). Then someone speaks up for the richness of human diversity and the individual wonders of separate peoples (and their theories get hijacked by racists). Perhaps we should take a generous and forgiving view. And then hunker down together to fight the next swarm of racists.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-04T14:15:38-07:00","id":1394148,"title":"","content":"I mean Campbell is undeniably racist, I don\u2019t see how one can deny that considering that exact quote Watcher linked. Pop culture may love his ideas, but that doesn\u2019t mean the idea that all religions and cultures are just lesser versions of some incredibly Eurocentric idea of a \u201cplatonic ideal of religion\u201d isn\u2019t incredibly racist and dismissive","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24769-magicjohnny","name":"Magicjohnny","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24769_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"152"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-04T17:26:15-07:00","id":1394192,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magicjohnny</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1392923-other-worlds-and-aliens-in-scion?p=1394148#post1394148\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean Campbell is undeniably racist, I don\u2019t see how one can deny that considering that exact quote Watcher linked. Pop culture may love his ideas, but that doesn\u2019t mean the idea that all religions and cultures are just lesser versions of some incredibly Eurocentric idea of a \u201cplatonic ideal of religion\u201d isn\u2019t incredibly racist and dismissive</div> </div> </div> </div>Why is the idea of human unity and an awareness of cultural exchange racist?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-04T18:22:59-07:00","id":1394204,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1392923-other-worlds-and-aliens-in-scion?p=1394192#post1394192\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Why is the idea of human unity and an awareness of cultural exchange racist?</div> </div> </div> </div>That is not the part <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24769-magicjohnny\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar24769_2.gif');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"24769\" data-vbnamecard=\"24769\">Magicjohnny</a> was calling racist.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Campbell</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Whether we listen with aloof amusement to the dreamlike mumbo jumbo of some red-eyed witch doctor of the Congo</div> </div> </div> </div>Is the quote I think Magicjohnny is referring too.<br /> <br /> As for the matter of Campbell himself...by your own account <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar857_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"857\" data-vbnamecard=\"857\">Astromancer</a>, by your own account, he grew up in an environment of 'gentile racism'.<br /> Regardless of his highest ideals moving away from that, by todays standards, some of his work may still contain elements of lingering biases' that are offensive to modern audiences.<br /> Which is not what this topic is about.<br /> <br /> Please don't get upset, but whether or not a historical figure is racist is...more of an issue of comparison degrees than yes or no. Was Campbell racist for his period and culture, less so than his peers. By modern standards, yes, though many of his contemporaries may well be much worse.<br /> <br /> Back on topic, does anyone have good ideas for alien Denizen Paths?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-04T18:45:40-07:00","id":1394208,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FallenEco</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1392923-other-worlds-and-aliens-in-scion?p=1394204#post1394204\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Back on topic, does anyone have good ideas for alien Denizen Paths?</div> </div> </div> </div>Missionary/Prophet might be a good one. Read &quot;In Advance of the Landing&quot; which documents religious reactions across the US and Canada to the UFO phenomenon. Seeing our &quot;Space Brothers&quot; as Prophets and religious teachers goes back to at least the 1950's.<br /> <br /> Many UFO contactees speak of being the target of bizarre tricks and brutal games. So both Trickster and Liminal seem right too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-04T19:10:33-07:00","id":1394212,"title":"","content":"Denizen path hm.<br /> <br /> Getting inspiration from mythologies my first idea would be a tzitzimime denizen path. It would be a ver titanspawnish one but i think it could be fun to play.<br /> <br /> The other idea im having, which could be a bit too out there, would be a constellation denizen path.<br /> In various mythologies animals, peoples and characters were transformed into constellation so considering they would keep their sentience and agency they could have pr make descendant.<br /> Im imagining someone that looks like a void with interconnected stars in the silhouette. <br /> Ive got nothing besides the aesthetics tho.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Completed campaign: Scion 2nd Edition. Les L\u00e9gendes Currently playing: Being a dad for a 3 year old daughter and a 2 years old son and now a beautiful new baby.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11312-maitrecorbo","name":"Maitrecorbo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11312_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"719"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-04T20:37:16-07:00","id":1394227,"title":"","content":"Running with Maitrecorbo's notion. Here are some ideas for different constellations.<br /> <br /> The Big and Little Bears hold the pole star and are two hunters transformed into bears and then stars. So both Guide and Hunter fit.<br /> <br /> Draco often has the pole star and was supposed to be the guardian of an Oracle. Sage and Guardian fit.<br /> <br /> Ask what the character did in their stories, that will give the paths.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}